1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,862
Search engines read a sitemap to find the pages of your site.

2
00:00:04,862 --> 00:00:07,860
This video covers two features for developers:

3
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:13,798
Localized Content Item Sitemaps, which adds language alternates, and Sitemaps for Decoupled Razor

4
00:00:13,798 --> 00:00:17,660
Pages, which lists content that your own Razor Pages display.

5
00:00:22,260 --> 00:00:27,836
For each content item, the Sitemap Content Types source of a sitemap needs two answers:

6
00:00:27,836 --> 00:00:30,774
is its type routeable, and what is its URL.

7
00:00:30,774 --> 00:00:35,750
Providers give both answers, and a coordinator asks them one after the other.

8
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:39,879
A provider implements IRouteableContentTypeProvider.

9
00:00:39,879 --> 00:00:44,539
It lists the content types it can route, and returns the route of an item.

10
00:00:44,539 --> 00:00:50,830
Autoroute supplies one for types with an Autoroute part, and the Razor Pages feature supplies another.

11
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:58,586
The feature depends on Content Localization and Sitemaps.

12
00:00:58,586 --> 00:01:00,392
It registers two services:

13
00:01:00,392 --> 00:01:05,247
a metadata provider that adds the language alternates, and a query provider that

14
00:01:05,247 --> 00:01:10,440
replaces the default IContentItemsQueryProvider, which selects the items of a sitemap.

15
00:01:11,190 --> 00:01:17,826
For each URL, the metadata provider looks among the queried items for the same localization set.

16
00:01:17,826 --> 00:01:23,096
It skips a localization excluded by its Sitemap Part, and adds an alternate

17
00:01:23,096 --> 00:01:27,130
link with the culture as hreflang and the route as href.

18
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:38,751
In Tools, Features, the feature is listed as Localized Content Item Sitemaps, with the identifier OrchardCore.ContentLocalization.Sitemaps.

19
00:01:38,751 --> 00:01:43,540
Searching for sitemaps lists it with the other sitemap features.

20
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,841
Let's open the sitemap.

21
00:01:46,841 --> 00:01:50,429
Each address starts with the Base url of the site settings.

22
00:01:50,429 --> 00:01:54,900
The English article lists an alternate link for English and one for French,

23
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,550
and the French article lists the same two.

24
00:01:58,023 --> 00:02:03,671
The root element declares the xhtml namespace, because the metadata provider supplies it.

25
00:02:03,671 --> 00:02:08,487
The links are written once per localization, so a page and its translations

26
00:02:08,487 --> 00:02:10,093
all list one another.

27
00:02:14,293 --> 00:02:18,739
The Autoroute provider only knows content types with an Autoroute part.

28
00:02:18,739 --> 00:02:23,473
A decoupled site routes its content with Razor Pages instead, so those items

29
00:02:23,473 --> 00:02:25,436
have no URL for the sitemap.

30
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:29,363
The Sitemaps for Decoupled Razor Pages feature fills that gap.

31
00:02:30,113 --> 00:02:33,793
Configure SitemapsRazorPagesOptions in Program.cs.

32
00:02:33,793 --> 00:02:39,773
ConfigureContentType takes the name of the content type, and PageName names the Razor

33
00:02:39,773 --> 00:02:41,613
Page that displays it.

34
00:02:42,363 --> 00:02:45,462
RouteValues builds the link to the page for each item.

35
00:02:45,462 --> 00:02:48,717
It must include the area of the page, which for a page of

36
00:02:48,717 --> 00:02:52,333
your web project is the name of the project, and the values that

37
00:02:52,333 --> 00:02:54,193
the route of the page expects.

38
00:02:54,943 --> 00:02:59,679
For each item, the provider calls RouteValues and asks the URL helper for

39
00:02:59,679 --> 00:03:01,297
the link to the page.

40
00:03:01,297 --> 00:03:07,233
A content type without an option returns no route, so the coordinator asks the next provider.

41
00:03:08,933 --> 00:03:14,593
Let's open the Sitemap Content Types source of the sitemap, and clear Index All Content Types.

42
00:03:14,593 --> 00:03:19,404
Select Content Types lists Decoupled Blog Post next to Article, although it has

43
00:03:19,404 --> 00:03:23,933
no Autoroute part, because the Razor Pages provider lists it as routeable.

44
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:29,830
In the sitemap, each post has the address that the Razor Pages provider

45
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:32,665
built from the page name and the route values.

46
00:03:32,665 --> 00:03:36,863
The type has no Localization part, so a post carries no language links.

47
00:03:41,063 --> 00:03:45,572
To route content another way, write your own provider and register it in

48
00:03:45,572 --> 00:03:49,272
the services of your module, as the Autoroute module does.

49
00:03:49,272 --> 00:03:52,683
The Sitemap Content Types source uses every provider.

50
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:57,060
List the types you route, and return the route of an item, starting

51
00:03:57,060 --> 00:03:58,253
with the Base url.

52
00:03:58,253 --> 00:04:01,731
Return null for a type you do not route, so that the coordinator

53
00:04:01,731 --> 00:04:03,173
asks the next provider.

54
00:04:05,173 --> 00:04:09,025
Both features build on the extension points of the Sitemaps module:

55
00:04:09,025 --> 00:04:14,250
providers that route content types, query providers that select items, and metadata providers

56
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:15,780
that complete each URL.

57
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:17,153
Thanks for watching.

